From af1c836e5ba49090af42c29109833436f4005dee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:36:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: qcom: sm8250: Xiaomi Mi 10T Pro (apollo) support

Everything needed on top of upstream to build the kernel for apollo, a
Xiaomi Mi 10T Pro (M2007J3SG) used as a headless k3s node, as one commit
so it can be rebased onto newer kernels.

Base: v7.2.8.
Source: royka1/linux branch apollo-7.1 at 71aebd11db5d (postmarketOS
community port), reduced to what the node configuration compiles. On
v7.1 the result was checked against royka1's tree built with the same
configuration: identical DTB, the same 542 modules and the same vmlinux
symbol count. Rebased onto v7.2.8: the two conflicts (pcie-qcom.c,
qcom_common.h) showed that royka1's PCIe changes serve only the modem,
so they are left out now, and apollo_defconfig turns off the pin and
clock controllers of other Qualcomm SoCs that 7.2 enables by default.
Two 7.2 API changes: the panel driver allocates with
devm_drm_panel_alloc() (drm_panel_init() is gone), and the Type-C
connector names the PM8150B VBUS regulator as its vbus-supply, where
7.2's driver looks for it now that pm8150b.dtsi no longer sets
vdd-vbus-supply (without it, source mode would get a dummy regulator).
Compared with the v7.1 build: the same modules apart from 7.2's own
crypto and module moves, and the same DTB apart from that supply and
upstream's sm8250.dtsi changes (PCIe iommu-map, Venus power domains).

Included:
- Device tree: sm8250-xiaomi-apollo.dts (PS_HOLD restart node for warm
  reboots, ramoops), the fork's sm8250.dtsi and pm8150/pm8150b/pm8150l
  changes, and the dtbs Makefile entry.
- Charging: the PM8150B SMB5 charger (qcom_pm8150b_charger) and the PMIC
  fuel gauge (qcom_fg), with the power_supply additions they use.
- Power key and reset: the vendor QPNP power-on driver, msm-poweroff
  changes, and SDAM power-loss breadcrumbs (apollo_breadcrumb,
  qcom-spmi-sdam).
- Display: the NT36675 panel, the LCDB bias regulator and DSI fixes, so
  the panel can show a console (the device tree has no simple-framebuffer).
- Wi-Fi (QCA6390): ath11k, MHI host and QRTR changes.
- Remote processors: SMP2P sleep-state notifier, sysmon, q6v5, PDR and
  the PD mapper; SCM additions.
- gpiolib-of and the of_gpio.h header the vendor drivers still use.
- arch/arm64/configs/apollo_defconfig: royka1's configuration plus the
  k3s/Cilium networking options, kernel BTF (full DWARF; Cilium's BPF
  masquerade needs it), CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-apollo", no built-in
  firmware, and without the modem, audio, camera and touch stacks.

Left out (not needed on a node, or other devices in the fork): the SDX55
modem over PCIe (MHI satellite, Sahara loader, boot logger, keep-alive,
esoc, IPA over MHI, pci_generic, and the PCIe link retrain/L23/PERST
helpers in pcie-qcom plus an MSI debug print), voice and audio (q6voice,
sm8250 sound changes, CS35L41 mapping, lpass pinctrl, APR), cameras
(sensors, VCMs, camss), FastRPC, the NT36523 touchscreen, the BQ25970
charge pump, other panels, the Lenovo, OnePlus and Xiaomi
pipa/elish/enuma device trees and the apollo camera overlay, the debugfs
overlay loader, tools/remoteproc and stray .orig files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
